Enhanced ground grass: ao-vk
============================

The optional Enhanced ground-grass renderer (crates/ao-render/src/grass.rs,
grass.wgsl, grass_noise.rs) ports algorithms and shader code from ao-vk's
procedural grass (rvk/grass.cpp, rvk/shaders/grass.vert, grass_common.glsl,
wind.glsl): the camera-facing four-section blade strips and their kinds (blade,
broad blade, seed stalk, flower), tuft clumping and fan-out, wildflower patches,
slope and path-edge thinning, root-to-tip shading with canopy darkening, light
through the blade, wind waves and gusts, the character push, the minimum
drawn blade width and the smooth distance thinning. Placement and colour are
driven by this project's own terrain data instead. No ao-vk artwork or binary
asset is used; the blades are generated procedurally at draw time.

